---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import ConfirmOfficial from "../components/ConfirmOfficial.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Andorra, without the brochure"
  description="A private guide to residency, companies, property and the professionals worth using in Andorra."
  path="/"
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <h1>Andorra, without the brochure</h1>
    <p>
      If you are deciding whether to move money and time to Andorra,
      start here. If you want a weekend in the mountains, this is the
      wrong site.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <ConfirmOfficial />
    <p>
      Andorra is a small country that sells a simple story: ten per cent
      tax, mountains, safety, Europe without being in the EU. The story
      is not false. It is incomplete. The permit is not the tax position.
      The house is not automatically the investment. The bank will not
      open because you asked nicely. And the 2026 law raised the price of
      arriving without working.
    </p>
    <p>
      Andorra Private is a short, maintained set of pages for people who
      are actually going to file. We keep the four decisions that cost
      real money in one place, and we keep a private list of
      professionals we would use. We do not list every plumber in
      Escaldes.
    </p>

    <h2>The four decisions</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Decision</th>
          <th>The question</th>
          <th>Read</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Permit</td>
          <td>Can you live here, and on what terms?</td>
          <td>
            <a href="/residency-vs-tax">Three things people confuse</a>
            and
            <a href="/passive-residency">Passive residency in 2026</a>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Tax</td>
          <td>Will Spain, France or the UK still treat you as theirs?</td>
          <td>
            <a href="/residency-vs-tax">Three things people confuse</a>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Company</td>
          <td>Do you need an Andorran SL, or only a permit?</td>
          <td>
            <a href="/company-active-residency">Company and active residency</a>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>House and bank</td>
          <td>Can you buy, and will a bank take you?</td>
          <td>
            <a href="/buying-property">Buying property</a>
            and
            <a href="/the-file">The file and the bank</a>
          </td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p>
      Most people arriving from Spain or France mix up three separate
      things: the immigration permit, tax residency, and buying a house.
      Mix them up and you can spend a million euros and still be tax
      resident somewhere you were trying to leave. Read
      <a href="/residency-vs-tax">Three things people confuse</a>
      before you read anything else.
    </p>

    <h2>What changed in 2026</h2>
    <p>
      Llei 2/2026 (Òmnibus 2) came into force on 13 February 2026. For
      new passive files the investment floor is generally one million
      euros in Andorran assets, with a property unit floor of eight
      hundred thousand if you use real estate. The AFA sum is, for new
      files, a payment rather than a refundable bond. Foreign buyers of
      property pay a higher investment tax than they did in 2024. Quotas
      exist. Treat any article dated before February 2026 as a historical
      document.
    </p>
    <p>
      The BOPA text is
      <a
        href="https://bopadocuments.blob.core.windows.net/bopa-documents/038015/pdf/CGL_2026_02_12_10_11_12.pdf"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Llei 2/2026</a
      >.
      Immigration pages sit on
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/immigracio/residencia"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Govern.ad</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>Who this is for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You can show serious means and a clean record.</li>
      <li>
        You can actually spend 90 or 183 days here, not just book a flat
        and leave.
      </li>
      <li>
        You want names, numbers and the points where files fail — not a
        mood board.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who this is not for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Anyone looking for a seven-day “golden visa” with no presence.
      </li>
      <li>Anyone who needs Andorra to pretend it is still 2019.</li>
      <li>
        Anyone who wants a complete business directory. That already
        exists, and it is not what we are building.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Next</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/residency-vs-tax">Three things people confuse</a>,
      then either
      <a href="/passive-residency">Passive residency in 2026</a>
      or
      <a href="/company-active-residency">Company and active residency</a>.
      The private shortlist is not filled yet. Official sites we have
      already sourced sit in the
      <a href="/directory">directory</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
